1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,600
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,110
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,010
I've been an HVAC tech

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:09,380
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,600
Crawling through attics
and crawlspaces

7
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,370
on my knees,

8
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:13,630
every single day.

9
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:14,730
I had my right knee

10
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,320
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:18,600
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:19,970
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:22,140
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,130
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:24,350
This is different.

16
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:25,130
Tight.

17
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:25,940
Full.

18
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,630
Like a band around the
joint

19
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,970
that never loosens.

20
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,000
And for two years I've

21
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,280
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,300
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,800
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,230
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,480
At three months,

26
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:38,400
give it six.

27
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:39,620
At six months,

28
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,990
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:42,020
At a year,

30
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,760
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,800
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,000
We went down the list.

33
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,290
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:48,490
Every session,

35
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,890
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:51,040
I got stronger.

37
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,520
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:52,578 --> 00:00:53,930
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:55,000
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:56,620
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:57,640
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,480
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,940
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:02,070
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:03,590
And after that, a second

46
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:04,790
operation to go back

47
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:06,170
in and do it over.

48
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,450
I said no.

49
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,980
Every morning I climbed
out

50
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:10,590
of the van at the first
call

51
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:11,780
and my knee felt like

52
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,590
a band was wrapped around
it,

53
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:16,140
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

54
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,930
Every morning I took
something

55
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:19,490
for it and went to work.

56
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,190
Couldn't do the stairs,

57
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:22,690
couldn't kneel in front of
a furnace

58
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:24,470
long enough to finish a
job,

59
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:25,800
couldn't crawl into an
attic

60
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,580
without stopping every two
minutes.

61
00:01:28,144 --> 00:01:29,810
The younger guys on my
crew started

62
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:31,510
taking the attic calls for
me.

63
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:33,020
Nobody said a word.

64
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:34,930
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:36,580
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:36,580 --> 00:01:37,550
like getting in the van

67
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:38,880
or up off the floor,

68
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,030
into a decision.

69
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,590
After a long and serious

70
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:42,910
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,530
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:45,710
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:47,130
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,780
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:51,500
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:52,750
No loosening,

77
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,940
no infection, nothing
wrong.

78
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,290
Only this time there

79
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:57,560
was no new number.

80
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,032
Nobody said give it
another six months.

81
00:02:00,072 --> 00:02:01,650
There was nothing left to
give it.

82
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,160
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,180
lot for a while.

84
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,400
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,730
Then explain this.

86
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:09,130
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

87
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:10,570
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,920
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

89
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:15,010
Everyone in the house was
asleep

90
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,890
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

91
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:17,940
with my leg up,

92
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:20,060
trying to find any angle
where

93
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:21,820
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

94
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:23,770
around my knee and
tightening.

95
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,550
I had a furnace install at
seven.

96
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,150
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

97
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,830
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

98
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,130
And I just thought,

99
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:33,650
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:35,030
Thirty years in this
trade,

101
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,190
and now I couldn't get

102
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,120
down on one knee.

103
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,690
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:40,550
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:41,670
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:42,760
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:43,510
And when I found one,

108
00:02:43,510 --> 00:02:44,520
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,830
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:47,680
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,690
out and went looking.

112
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,080
Not for a product.

113
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,360
For an explanation.

114
00:02:51,610 --> 00:02:53,260
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,570
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:58,240
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:02:58,770 --> 00:03:00,830
And that's when I found a
video

118
00:03:00,830 --> 00:03:02,670
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

119
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:05,170
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

120
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:07,240
had been through exactly
this.

121
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:09,430
But before I say anything
else,

122
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,650
I want to be straight with
you.

123
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,750
You've already had
something work fast.

124
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,850
The ice.

125
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:15,500
The first week of a new
pill.

126
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:17,450
The good day after a
session.

127
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,754
Then it wore off.

128
00:03:18,794 --> 00:03:21,150
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

129
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,720
Fast relief

130
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,760
isn't relief.

131
00:03:24,010 --> 00:03:25,120
It's a preview.

132
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,270
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:27,810
you this works fast.

134
00:03:27,850 --> 00:03:28,720
It doesn't.

135
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:30,900
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:31,940
and to look at what's
going

137
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,360
on around your new knee

138
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,870
instead of inside it,

139
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:36,490
there is a real reason

140
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:37,750
it still hurts.

141
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,650
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,360
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,740
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:43,910
everything for me.

145
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,880
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,550
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:49,210
the worn joint surfaces

148
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,110
and puts in metal and
plastic.

149
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:53,220
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,890
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:57,000
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:59,010
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:59,010 --> 00:04:00,530
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:04:00,670 --> 00:04:01,090
He said,

155
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:02,570
think about a swollen foot

156
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:03,820
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:05,310
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,630
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:09,590
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:11,290
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:12,860
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,350
in a limited space

163
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,660
with living tissue packed
all around it.

164
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,710
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:20,420
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,320
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,940
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,780
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,310
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,150
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:31,150 --> 00:04:32,890
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:33,090 --> 00:04:34,300
So when you bend,

173
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:35,840
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:36,870
When you straighten,

175
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:38,020
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,370
That's the band.

177
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:41,440
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:42,400
And you start being

179
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,300
the one who says,

180
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,170
you go ahead.

181
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:45,160
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:46,860
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,510
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:50,500
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,370
around the knee.

186
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:52,450
Worth doing,

187
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:53,320
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,850
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:54,850 --> 00:04:55,930
taking up room.

190
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:57,270
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:57,270 --> 00:04:58,840
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:01,310
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,230
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:04,810
finally calms down,

195
00:05:04,810 --> 00:05:06,240
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,810
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,370
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:11,250
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:12,970
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,810
After two years of this,

201
00:05:14,810 --> 00:05:16,390
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:18,640
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,670
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,520
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:25,030
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:27,000
I'd bought knee pads,

207
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,640
knee sleeves, compression
braces,

208
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,210
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,530
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:34,570
me was an hour.

211
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:35,920
I even looked at going

212
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:36,940
to a clinic

213
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,290
for the light therapy.

214
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,560
But at $200 a session

215
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,860
with nothing covered by
insurance,

216
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,320
that was a quick no.

217
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,890
Then one night I went

218
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:47,240
back to that knee
replacement

219
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:49,230
group and actually read
it.

220
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,770
Thousands of people,

221
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:52,510
years out from surgery,

222
00:05:52,510 --> 00:05:54,840
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

223
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,130
nobody could explain.

224
00:05:56,310 --> 00:05:58,220
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

225
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,170
the same thing kept coming
up.

226
00:06:00,410 --> 00:06:02,030
This one device,

227
00:06:02,030 --> 00:06:03,670
and people saying it was
the first

228
00:06:03,670 --> 00:06:05,010
thing that made a
difference.

229
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:08,430
And before anyone jumps in
thinking, alright,

230
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,550
here it comes,

231
00:06:09,550 --> 00:06:11,100
he's selling me something,

232
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,960
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,320
I'm only here because I

234
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,010
made myself a promise

235
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:17,550
at 2:30 in the morning

236
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:18,760
that if I ever found

237
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,970
something that helped,

238
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:20,960
I'd say so.

239
00:06:21,090 --> 00:06:22,970
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:22,970 --> 00:06:24,530
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:24,770 --> 00:06:27,030
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:27,090 --> 00:06:28,890
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:31,180
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:33,590
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:34,550
just to see what all

246
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:35,610
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,470
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:41,780
charge $200 a session for,
off machines

249
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:44,180
that cost fifty thousand
dollars,

250
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,260
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,530
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,570
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,730
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:53,170
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:55,100
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:56,520
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:58,280
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,260
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,440
Ninety days.

260
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,660
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,020
no questions,

262
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,430
no store credit,

263
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:08,160
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,060
No physical therapist

265
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,420
ever gave me ninety days

266
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:12,720
to change my mind.

267
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,520
There wasn't much to lose,

268
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:15,470
so I ordered it.

269
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:17,070
Two of them, actually.

270
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,310
Only the right knee was
replaced,

271
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:21,120
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

272
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,990
and I'd done it for two
years.

273
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,080
The left one was carrying
the difference.

274
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:26,000
When it came,

275
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,050
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

276
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:29,100
because I'd been let down

277
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,850
too many times to get
excited.

278
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,480
What I felt was warmth.

279
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,010
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

280
00:07:35,230 --> 00:07:36,890
More like it was coming
from inside

281
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:38,650
the knee and spreading
around it.

282
00:07:39,030 --> 00:07:39,820
And that was it.

283
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:41,540
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:42,940
When I took it off,

285
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:43,850
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:43,850 --> 00:07:45,680
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:47,270
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,970
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,030
What was different

290
00:07:50,030 --> 00:07:51,130
was that for the first
time

291
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:52,670
in two years I'd done
something

292
00:07:52,670 --> 00:07:54,380
for my knee instead of to
it.

293
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:55,790
Twenty minutes,

294
00:07:55,790 --> 00:07:56,770
in my own chair,

295
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:57,630
after work.

296
00:07:57,670 --> 00:07:58,680
No drive,

297
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,600
no copay.

298
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:00,900
They say twenty minutes.

299
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:02,180
I did thirty,

300
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,130
twice a day,

301
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:05,160
lowest setting that first
week.

302
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:06,550
I put it on the calendar.

303
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:07,240
The first week,

304
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,080
I couldn't have told

305
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,590
you if anything was
happening.

306
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,400
I tried not to get

307
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,260
my hopes up.

308
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:12,330
I'd had things help

309
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:13,490
for a week and then stop.

310
00:08:13,530 --> 00:08:15,230
But somewhere in the
second week

311
00:08:15,230 --> 00:08:16,160
I noticed I'd come down

312
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,870
the stairs without holding
the rail.

313
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,570
I hadn't decided to.

314
00:08:19,610 --> 00:08:20,930
I just did it, then
stopped

315
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:22,760
halfway down because I
realized.

316
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:24,640
By the end of the fourth
week

317
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:26,060
I'd slept through the
night

318
00:08:26,060 --> 00:08:27,250
four times running.

319
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:28,550
I stood at the counter

320
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,110
and finished making dinner

321
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:31,520
without looking for the
stool.

322
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:33,450
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:33,490 --> 00:08:34,400
All of it was gone

324
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,490
for two years.

325
00:08:35,670 --> 00:08:37,270
A few weeks later my wife
asked

326
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:38,220
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,800
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:40,050 --> 00:08:41,000
And for the first time

329
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,910
in two years,

330
00:08:41,910 --> 00:08:43,020
I said yes.

331
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,310
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:46,750
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,650
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,690
One.

335
00:08:49,890 --> 00:08:51,740
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:54,920
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:56,050
Two.

338
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:59,180
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,280
so it takes up more

340
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,530
room than it should.

341
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:02,230
Three.

342
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:04,310
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:05,930
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:07,800
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,430
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:09,650 --> 00:09:10,380
Four.

347
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,980
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:15,240
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,490
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:17,710
can come down with it.

351
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:19,630
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:21,250
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:23,540
a knee replacement had
less pain,

354
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:25,150
less swelling and better
early

355
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:27,080
movement than those who
weren't.

356
00:09:27,410 --> 00:09:29,980
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:31,210
and was clear the evidence

358
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:32,260
is still limited.

359
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,250
I probably sound like a
broken record

360
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:35,590
to the guys on my crew.

361
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:37,770
But after two years of
doing everything

362
00:09:37,770 --> 00:09:39,840
I was told and getting
nowhere,

363
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,360
you have no idea

364
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,450
what it's like to sleep

365
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,210
through the night,

366
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:44,720
say yes to the walk,

367
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,170
and get my life back.

368
00:09:46,270 --> 00:09:47,490
So take it from me.

369
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,290
Don't spend another year
waiting

370
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:50,320
for it to settle.

371
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,230
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

372
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,800
More than ten thousand
people

373
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,860
with pain after a knee

374
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:57,030
replacement have already
tried this.

375
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:59,060
Some had it worse than I
did.

376
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,590
You can get the KenRelief

377
00:10:00,590 --> 00:10:02,280
wrap from their website,

378
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,560
with a discount link

379
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,290
and ninety days to try it.

380
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:07,870
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

381
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:09,160
you get your money back

382
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,560
and you keep the wrap.

383
00:10:10,990 --> 00:10:12,640
They only release so many

384
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:13,900
at that price.

385
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:15,190
If it's still there,

386
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:16,120
get one,

387
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,627
and stop the squeeze.

